"""Freeze bounded physical readings from full-sector raw plots and deciding checks."""
import csv,json
from pathlib import Path
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
Q=list(csv.DictReader((B/'queue.csv').open(newline='',encoding='utf-8')))
# physical verdict, period, epoch, depth, evidence, limits, next check
V={
'H031':('REFUTED','','','','The sector-94 dip at BTJD 3874.77 is simultaneous and similarly shaped in widely separated TIC 320328447 (H040): half-day bins put both about 6 ppt low near 3874.5-3875.0. The sector-103 dip and brightening are opposite sides of a large gap/offset followed by a decay, rather than a second resolved eclipse. Full raw sectors 13,27,67,94,101-104 show no repeat of the s94 event at either Gaia edge-on conjunction kind.','This refutes the selected repeat-eclipse interpretation; common-mode coincidence is diagnostic, not a proof of the exact instrument mechanism. It does not rule out a weaker unrelated eclipse.','Reinspect with independent photometry only if a distinct repeat emerges.'),
'H032':('PROBABLE','28.24465','','30','Deep flat-bottomed events recur in raw SAP sectors 12,39,66,93,103,104; a shallower kind occurs about 14 days away in several sectors. Independent local centers of the deep kind at 2379.6308,3113.9838,4159.0606,4187.2683 BTJD fit cycles 0,26,63,64 at about 28.24465 d; adjacent sectors 103/104 rule out nearby integer-cycle alternatives from the long baseline. Both kinds approximately match Gaia eccentric-orbit conjunctions for P=28.249018 d. A separate 5x5 TESSCut sector-66 extraction recovers a 29.53 ppt deep dip and an 8.15 ppt shallow dip.','Target attribution is unresolved: Gaia DR3 5923328421736889728, G=14.81, lies 6.36 arcsec away, approximate G flux ratio 0.045, and could supply a 30 ppt blended dip with a deep intrinsic eclipse. Difference centroids 0.108 and 0.264 pixel from the target do not deblend at 0.31 pixel separation. Clock and depth are exploratory, without calibrated errors; TESSCut shares photons with QLP. The bulk fold screen attempted P=28.24275 d but did not flag it (z=1.485); this review does not establish why.','Obtain resolved photometry of both eclipse kinds or a calibrated pixel-level blend fit.'),
'H033':('REFUTED','','','','All six raw sectors 7,8,34,35,61,88 show rapid quasi-periodic 1-2 day oscillations with changing amplitude and large brightenings, not isolated matched eclipse profiles. The dip and bright flags select phases of this broad oscillatory signal; Gaia conjunction windows do not show a stable repeated dip kind.','The selected eclipse interpretation is refuted by the full morphology; the source/mechanism of the oscillation is not determined.','Study the pulsation/rotation-like variability separately if useful.'),
'H034':('REFUTED','','','','The sector-25 2007.53 dip is a sparse shallow downturn followed by a bright point; the sector-86 3637.23 dip is the onset of an abrupt lower state at a data discontinuity. The full nine-sector raw curves include large slow rises and gap recoveries, and no stable 28.851 d eclipse kind repeats at the covered Gaia conjunction windows.','Refutation applies to the selected repeated eclipse interpretation, not every possible weaker signal. The sector-25 few-cadence structure has limited timing information.','Check a future clean conjunction only if a distinct feature is found.'),
'H035':('REFUTED','','','','Seven full raw sectors show smooth multi-day rises/falls and sector discontinuities. The retained s61/s88 dip windows and bright flags fall on slopes or opposite sides of gaps; no isolated repeated eclipse morphology appears at covered Gaia P=38.612 d conjunctions.','Selected eclipse interpretation is refuted; the broad variability remains unassigned.','Characterize broad variability using a stable aperture if desired.'),
'H036':('REFUTED','','','','The six raw sectors 9,10,36,63,90,99 display repeating broad multi-day waves whose shape and phase evolve. Selected sector-63 and sector-99 dips are troughs in those waves, and bright flags are crests. They are not resolved ingress, flat bottom and egress of a 42.033 d eclipse kind.','Selected eclipse interpretation is refuted; modulation could be astrophysical but is not classified here.','Analyze the broad modulation separately if useful.'),
'H037':('REFUTED','','','','The strongest sector-100 dip at BTJD 4087.97 begins at a discontinuous lower segment after a gap and then recovers monotonically. The sector-101 4105.96 depression is broad low-level evolution before a step. Other raw sectors 12,27,66,93,101,103 lack the same isolated shape at covered Gaia conjunctions.','Refutes the selected two-sector eclipse claim; gaps prevent using these features as precise nulls for any other hidden signal.','Seek a clean future event if a separate eclipse signature appears.'),
'H038':('REFUTED','','','','The sector-64 3056.52 dip lies on a strong descending trend that crosses a gap/offset; sector-65 3081.76 is likewise a sloping trough before a gap and abrupt high state. Full sectors 38,64,65,99-101 show evolving multi-day structure rather than repeated isolated eclipse profiles near 41.891 d Gaia conjunctions.','Selected repeat-eclipse interpretation is refuted; broad variability has no assigned physical cause.','Use stable independent photometry if studying the broader variation.'),
'H039':('PLAUSIBLE','','','','A single asymmetric ~15 ppt sector-12 raw dip reaches a minimum near BTJD 1625.85 and recovers over several days. A separate TESSCut 5x5 aperture preserves the feature, while the QLP corrected KSPSAP flux suppresses it. The raw series starts at 1624.97, only ~0.9 d before minimum, so there is no secure pre-event baseline; the eight currently available sectors equal the eight cached sectors and show no comparable repeat. The event is ~9 days from the Gaia 29.729 d conjunction prediction, so Gaia does not supply a secure eclipse clock.','A single event near sector start could be a real eclipse or startup/systematic. A Gaia G=13.72 source 5.96 arcsec away is flux-capable at approximate G flux ratio 0.053; WCS/aperture evidence does not locate the source. No period, epoch or depth is promoted to a system measurement.','Obtain a complete repeat with pre- and post-event baseline and resolved photometry.'),
'H040':('REFUTED','','','','The sector-94 3874.77 dip is simultaneous with a near-identical feature in H031, a target several degrees away; both are ~6 ppt low in the same half-day bin. The sector-101 4108.09 dip is a lower state after a gap with a slow recovery and no eclipse boundaries. Full raw sectors 13,27,67,94,101,103 lack a consistent 20.664 d eclipse kind.','Selected repeat-eclipse interpretation is refuted; this does not prove the target has no unseen eclipse. Current TESSCut inventory also lists sector 104 beyond cached QLP, but that cannot make the two positive features resolved eclipses.','Inspect new photometry if a distinct isolated event emerges.'),
}
fields=['sample_id','tic','sample_stratum','physical_verdict','full_review_completion','novelty_status','period_days','period_error_days','primary_epoch_btjd','depth_ppt','limitations','next_check','report']
rows=[]
for q in Q:
 sid=q['sample_id'];tic=q['tic'];v,p,e,d,evidence,limits,nextcheck=V[sid]
 src=json.loads((B/tic/'raw-inspection.json').read_text());sectors=[s['sector'] for s in src['sectors'] if 'path' in s]
 t=(f'# {sid} — TIC {tic}\n\nPhysical verdict: **{v}**. Bounded review: **COMPLETE**. Catalogue novelty: **UNKNOWN** because four VizieR gates were unavailable; a primary-table nonmatch is not novelty clearance.\n\n'
    f'Gaia DR3 {q["gaia_dr3"]}, {q["nss_type"]}, orbital P={float(q["gaia_period_days"]):.5f} d. Frozen stratum `{q["sample_stratum"]}`; sample ID is not a physical acceptance. Raw SAP with QUALITY=0 inspected for sectors {", ".join(map(str,sectors))}.\n\n'
    f'## Deciding evidence\n\n{evidence}\n\n## Limits and next check\n\n{limits} {nextcheck}\n\n'
    f'## Sources\n\n`raw-inspection.json` includes verified bulk/FITS SHA-256 receipts and representative flagged-window numbers; `raw-windows.png` plots those windows. `orbit-context.json` and `.png` show every cached sector with approximate Gaia edge-on conjunctions. Screening centers are not measured eclipse centers. The frozen [source packet](../../source-packets/{tic}/sources.json), [central catalogue record](../../shared-catalogues/target-evidence.json), batch scripts and manifest preserve provenance.\n')
 if sid in ('H031','H040'):t+='\n[Shared sector-94 raw comparison](../common-event.json) gives matched timestamps and bin medians. `alternate-s94.json`/`.png` show local raw SAP diagnostics.\n'
 if sid=='H032':t+='\n[Helper timing and alias audit](../helper-clock.json), [local fits](../helper-local-fits.json), [pixel attribution](../helper-source-attribution.json), [shallow-kind attribution](../helper-shallow-attribution.json), and `../helper-pixels/372989764/` contain independent extraction and WCS receipts. `alternate-s66.json` adds raw local diagnostics.\n'
 if sid=='H039':t+='\n`alternate-s12.json`/`.png` compare SAP with QLP corrected KSPSAP and background/centroid diagnostics. [Helper pixel extraction](../helper-pixels/454228598/) and [Gaia neighbors](../helper-h039-neighbors.json) preserve the independent aperture and close-source assessment. `sector-availability.raw` records the current TESSCut sector response.\n'
 if sid in ('H031','H040'):t+='\n`sector-availability.raw` records the current TESSCut sector response.\n'
 (B/tic/'REPORT.md').write_text(t,encoding='utf-8')
 rows.append(dict(sample_id=sid,tic=tic,sample_stratum=q['sample_stratum'],physical_verdict=v,full_review_completion='COMPLETE',novelty_status='UNKNOWN',period_days=p,period_error_days='',primary_epoch_btjd=e,depth_ppt=d,limitations=limits,next_check=nextcheck,report=str((B/tic/'REPORT.md').resolve())))
with (B/'RESULTS.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf-8') as f:
 w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=fields);w.writeheader();w.writerows(rows)
print({v:sum(x['physical_verdict']==v for x in rows) for v in sorted({x['physical_verdict'] for x in rows})})
